e: I'd say around 65-70. It's directionally correct and addresses a real need, but the framing gaps and missing compliance-specific elements keep it from being a full solution. From my vantage point, it's promising but not something I'd \"back without hesitation\" because it doesn't fully address audit readiness, data protection in logs, or post-lifetime retention.\n\nLet me settle on 68.\n",
