oject rather than something that pushes technical boundaries. It solves a real problem efficiently. The \"custom template engine\" part is slightly over-stated (it's really just templating), which suggests some mild scope ambiguity. Also, the focus on PDFs as the output format is somewhat limiting — regulatory authorities may want structured data (JSON, XML) in addition to human-readable documents for machine-checking. But these are minor concerns.\n\nI'll go with 80.\n",
