gulatory obligation (technical documentation under Recital 71 / Article 11 by extension)\n- It reduces compliance risk of documentation gaps\n- But as scoped, it's incomplete for full compliance (lifetime coverage, human oversight, audit trails)\n- The \"real-time during validation\" limitation is concerning for a lifetime requirement\n\nI think this clears my bar as a proposal worth pursuing, but with the understanding that the scope needs to be expanded. The core concept is sound and directly maps to regulatory requirements. However, I'm somewhat concerned about the \"automated\" framing without human review, and the validation-only focus.\n\nDecision: I'll approve it because the core mechanism (extracting metadata from training runs → generating compliance documentation) directly serves Article 12/Recital 71 obligations, and the integration with existing tools makes it feasible. But my promise score should reflect that as scoped, it's incomplete for full regulatory coverage.\n\nPromise: I'd say around 68-72. It addresses a real compliance need, uses existing infrastructure (lower implementation risk), and directly maps to Recital 71. But the validation-only scope, lack of human review mechanism, and \"automated\" without oversight are concerns that limit my confidence in it fully satisfying the regulatory requirement as written. I'll go with 70.\n",
