tended to include those specific fields. The proposal as stated doesn't explicitly mention all required log fields for Annex III 1(a) systems, which is a concern but not fatal since it's described as a \"framework\" and \"library.\"\n\nOverall: This is a high-value compliance infrastructure investment. It directly addresses the core obligation of Article 12(1) - automatic recording capability. The standardized approach reduces per-project compliance risk significantly. I would approve this, though I'd note that implementation must ensure full coverage of Article 12(2) and (3) requirements, not just timestamps.\n\nPromise score: This is very strong from a compliance perspective. It's the kind of systemic control that regulators look favorably upon. The main risk is incomplete implementation scope (missing some specific log fields), but as a framework/library it can be extended. I'd say 82-85. Let me settle on 83 - strong approval with the caveat that the actual implementation must cover all Article 12(3) minimum requirements, not just timestamps and input references.\n",
