ant deployments. From my compliance vantage point, this is exactly the kind of structural control I want in place. The minor concern about specificity of what \"compliant\" means for logging checks is addressable during implementation and doesn't undermine the core value.\n\nI would approve this with a high promise score. It's not a 100 because the proposal as stated could be more specific about validating the particular data elements required by Article 12(3), but the architecture and intent are sound and directly serve my compliance mandate. I'd put it around 85-90.\n\nLet me settle on 87 - strong alignment with my mandate, concrete implementation path, minor gaps in specificity that can be addressed during build-out but don't undermine the core value proposition.\n",
