sessment:**\nThe concept is sound and addresses a real compliance need. The architectural pattern (centralized logging via middleware/API wrappers) is proven in industry. However, from my prototyping speed perspective, the \"unified\" and \"centralized\" aspects introduce coupling and potential bottlenecks. The proposal is somewhat high-level and doesn't address the hard technical challenges of fitting diverse AI architectures into a single interception layer.\n\nI think this clears my bar - it's technically viable as a direction, addresses a real requirement, and the core pattern is sound. But I have significant concerns about execution details that affect prototyping speed. It's a good proposal but not a \"100/100 without hesitation\" because of the coupling risks and architectural vagueness around how it handles diverse system types.\n\nI'd say: approve, with a promise score around 72-78. The core idea is right and technically feasible, but the execution challenges (diverse architectures, performance impact, prototyping flexibility) prevent me from giving it a higher score. It's solid infrastructure work that would genuinely help compliance while reducing researcher burden, if executed well.\n",
