erate promise — it's directionally right and resource-efficient in the long run, but the implementation path described (integrating into core model architecture as mandatory dependency) could be expensive and constraining for an R&D lab. The \"without degrading performance\" claim is a red flag from my perspective because it suggests they haven't fully costed the engineering effort.\n\nI'll approve it with a moderate-to-high promise score, maybe 68-72. It's necessary, efficient in principle, but the implementation as described has costs and risks that make me want to be measured rather than enthusiastic. Let me settle on 70 — I'd back this direction but would push for a phased approach and assessment of existing infrastructure first.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The proposal says \"integrate a logging API into the core model architecture\" — for an R&D lab, modifying core model architecture is expensive and risky. A more efficient approach might be sidecar/observability-layer integration rather than architectural modification. But the proposal as stated doesn't specify this level of detail. The direction is right; the implementation path needs scrutiny.\n\nI'll go with approve at 70.\n",
