lly solve the regulatory requirement.\n\nI'm leaning toward reject or low-score approve. Let me think more carefully...\n\nActually, from my vantage point specifically (technical viability and prototyping speed/quality):\n- The technical approach is viable for what it claims to do (extract metadata, generate reports).\n- It's a reasonable prototype to build quickly given existing infra.\n- BUT: the core deliverable (compliance with Article 12) is not well-addressed by this tool. The actual logging infrastructure needs are runtime concerns, not dev-time metadata extraction.\n- As a standalone proposal to commit scarce implementation resources to, it's building a tool that doesn't actually solve the regulatory problem it claims to address.\n\nI'll reject it. It's a nice-to-have for documentation workflow but misidentifies what Article 12 requires. The promise score should reflect that while the prototyping approach is sound, the alignment with actual requirements is poor. I'd say around 30-40 - technically feasible and quick to prototype, but doesn't hit the mark for what's actually needed.\n\nLet me settle on: reject, promise 35.\n",
